text.section:
As used in this section, a customer's "identification document" means any of the following:

A state-issued driver's license or identification card;


A U.S. government resident alien identification card;


A passport;


A U.S. military identification card;


A Non-U.S. government identification card;


A Mexican Matricula identification card; or


Other government identification card.

A registrant shall not cash an item for a customer in the course of conducting its business unless the registrant:

Makes a copy of both sides of the item or maintains a record of the following information that is available from the item:
				a. ABA number;
				b. Account number;
				c. Check number;
				d. Check type;
				e. Date of check; and
				f. Check amount; and


Makes a copy of an identification document that is presented by the customer to the registrant at the time the customer presents the item for cashing or maintains a record of the following information that is available from the identification:
				a. Name;
				b. Address;
				c. Date of birth;
				d. Type of identification;
				e. Identification number; and
				f. Identification expiration date.
